    "descriptionModule": {
      "briefSummary": "The goal of this clinical study is to learn if adding a medicine called cilostazol to usual treatment can help prevent another stroke, a heart attack, or death in patients who had a stroke caused by a blocked blood vessel, or a \"mini-stroke\" (also called a TIA), in the past 6 months.\n\nTo determine if cilostazol is safe and effective at lowering the chance of strokes, heart attacks and deaths, the study will compare cilostazol to a placebo, a pill that looks the same as cilostazol but has no medicine in it.\n\nParticipants will:\n\n* Be assigned by chance to take either cilostazol or a placebo, along with their usual medicine.\n* Not know which one they are taking, and neither will the study team, which keeps the results fair.\n* Be followed for up to 5 years to see if they have a stroke, heart attack, or major bleeding."
    },
